{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again","id":1289791,"title":"Why bring back the Tell, again?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-19T21:09:18-08:00","id":1289791,"title":"Why bring back the Tell, again?","content":"In my experience with previous editions, the Tell mechanic has always been at best kind of annoying. This one looks poised to repeat that: it's got the same fiddly thing going on where high enough rolls can see through it regardless of shape, until a minor investment then negates it entirely most of the time. In practice, this just makes the Charm to hide an obligatory tax for characters that ever plan to do social infiltration stuff, while others just won't care most of the time. On top of that, the GM will be stuck keeping track of who has or hasn't seen through it for individual PCs whenever recurring NPCs come up.<br /> <br /> Like, what's the reason to even include it? What do the game and its themes actually gain in play from forcing characters to have a distinctive quality that, broadly speaking, either they'll immediately suppress from character creation or they'll never care about enough to interact with mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:14:20-08:00","id":1289795,"title":"","content":"One of the most basic things people ever seem to want from Lunars is emulation of shapeshifting narratives in myth and folklore.<br /> <br /> A really common (and in my opinion, compelling) element in shapeshifting narratives in myth and folklore is some innocuous recurring trait that can alternately give the shapeshifter away, or be a moment of dawning horror that is the prelude to the masquerade being dropped in the worst way possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:23:18-08:00","id":1289797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289795#post1289795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most basic things people ever seem to want from Lunars is emulation of shapeshifting narratives in myth and folklore.<br /> <br /> A really common (and in my opinion, compelling) element in shapeshifting narratives in myth and folklore is some innocuous recurring trait that can alternately give the shapeshifter away, or be a moment of dawning horror that is the prelude to the masquerade being dropped in the worst way possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's already a mechanic for doing that kind of thing in a way that won't just get ignored at first opportunity by players: Perfected Hybrid Interaction. Why have the recurring cross-form traits that players will actually care about using, <b>and</b> the recurring cross-form traits that players will immediately try to suppress because they promptly make a bunch of social stuff impossible, so that the players and GM have to keep track of both at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","user":"Roadie","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:23:56-08:00","id":1289798,"title":"","content":"At this point there are only a few times when the tell matters. You hit bonfire or above or you get hit by eye of the unconquered sun or some equivalent detection spell if you purchase one charm. The tell isn't a big deal but it does exist to counterbalance free stealth and was there in the first place due to how myths works with certain famous shapeshifters. But again one charm and pretty much the only thing that detects it is the eye of the unconquered sun..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:32:48-08:00","id":1289800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289798#post1289798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point there are only a few times when the tell matters. You hit bonfire or above or you get hit by eye of the unconquered sun or some equivalent detection spell if you purchase one charm. The tell isn't a big deal but it does exist to counterbalance free stealth and was there in the first place due to how myths works with certain famous shapeshifters. But again one charm and pretty much the only thing that detects it is the eye of the unconquered sun..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of my complaint. If it's that easy to get and that effective, and with how it overwhelmingly applies to the entire field of social ability in a way more fundamental than even excellencies, the obvious assumption is that any character who cares about it even a little bit will buy it. At that point why even have it, rather than reducing the number of Charms by 1 and combining its effects into the base write-up of the Tell?<br /> <br /> Of course, that's leaving aside how you're spending a Charm on making your character less worse, rather than making the character better, because the chargen mechanics leave you in a hole you have to fill in before you can reliably use your other primary abilities on social interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:34:56-08:00","id":1289802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289797#post1289797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there's already a mechanic for doing that kind of thing in a way that won't just get ignored at first opportunity by players: Perfected Hybrid Interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Perfected Hybrid Interaction really models the narrative effectively, because the onus on it being present in a scene is entirely on the Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why have the recurring cross-form traits that players will actually care about using</div> </div> </div> </div>So you have a version that is actually leveraged for mechanical baggage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the recurring cross-form traits that players will immediately try to suppress because they promptly make a bunch of social stuff impossible</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're giving a lot of credit to the characters of the setting to widely afford them Perception + Awareness rolls that can hit difficulty 7.<br /> <br /> Like, even for people who have seen the Lunar flare their anima enough to become familiar with the Tell, the majority of the characters in the setting can't reliably roll four successes. If one is going a few levels deeper into the diegesis, I would presume that Awareness is one of the least commonly cultivated Abilities among normal people.<br /> <br /> Presuming somebody who doesn't have magical enhancement to seeing through disguises, the only way that keeping your Tell under wraps without further magic is impossible is if you're meeting with one of the most observant people in Creation, who has already seen your Tell before in the past, and you're doing a really terrible job of acting like the person you're pretending to be.<br /> <br /> Good Lord, a Lunar who conducts themselves like that deserves to be found out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">so that the players and GM have to keep track of both at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel as though the player who is unveiling a mutation with a Charm has decided to forego discretion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:38:29-08:00","id":1289803,"title":"","content":"Because being able to spot a shapeshifter is an element in folklore and fiction. The Tell rules make it difficult enough but still possible that it's only going to happen with truly epic, plot relevant characters (like other PCs) to get that plot point without kneecapping shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:42:49-08:00","id":1289805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289800#post1289800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that's leaving aside how you're spending a Charm on making your character less worse, rather than making the character better, because the chargen mechanics leave you in a hole you have to fill in before you can reliably use your other primary abilities on social interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see a disconnect in priorities here.<br /> <br /> The Tell is meant to be a liability by design. For people that are playing Lunars, it's not meant to be a very large liability, but still one that some considerations need to be made around, which can add an edge of tension and excitement to the subject of shapeshifting and flaring their anima. For people that are not playing Lunars, it's meant to be a liability that can help them with realising that they're looking at a Lunar, so that shapeshifting doesn't let them always act with impunity or get the drop on people.<br /> <br /> It's not the only thing in the game meant to act as a narratively interesting liability. Look at the fact that you're required to give your character a Defining Intimacy. Sure, that one carries a converse benefit, but you still end up with something that can knock a big chunk out of your Resolve and leave you open to being compelled to doing some very extreme things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:53:06-08:00","id":1289806,"title":"","content":"That being said, having now had the opportunity to see the mechanics of the Tell alongside Subtle Silver Declaration, putting the Charm's benefits into context... it does feel like a liability that is a bit too easy to close off entirely. I had half a mind to raise concern about it being mandatory to close off that liability if you were going into Appearance's subterfuge Charms, but... I suppose if you're dedicating yourself to subterfuge powers, that kind of hole in your disguises ends up being the last thing you want.<br /> <br /> {checks the Charm again} Sorry, wasn't fully reading the thing. The liability is not completely closed off, people who have seen your Tell before (probably exposed by anima) can still roll to detect it. I would want to find clarification on whether or not they still get the three automatic successes. For the time being, I'm satisfied with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:01:29-08:00","id":1289821,"title":"","content":"Why? Because it's thematic and cool, and because any plot involving masters of disguise is already going to involve bookkeeping about who has and hasn't made you before (in this or any other disguise). Giving Lunars mechanics to play with that is just an extension of their schtick as shapeshifting tricksters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:06:10-08:00","id":1289822,"title":"","content":"Another thing that i think goes unnoticed and unrecognised is that the Lunar tell is intended to be very subtle; we see mechanics for noticing it and go &quot;how can these be that good of shapeshifters with a way to spot them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mara changes her shape and no matter what shape she takes, she has goat legs. However a neomah appears, there is always a demonic aspect. But the lack of unique and special mechanics to notice obvious elements like this, I think, paradoxically makes them seem less noticable to players. There's a roll to notice, therefore it's more obvious than the lady with goat legs, who can only hide them by wearing a floor length skirt and hoping you don't notice the clip-clop of hooves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 02-20-2019, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:12:32-08:00","id":1289825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289822#post1289822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that i think goes unnoticed and unrecognised is that the Lunar tell is intended to be very subtle; we see mechanics for noticing it and go &quot;how can these be that good of shapeshifters with a way to spot them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mara changes her shape and no matter what shape she takes, she has goat legs. However a neomah appears, there is always a demonic aspect. But the lack of mechanics to notice obvious elements like this, I think, paradoxically makes them seem less noticable to players. There's a roll to notice, therefore it's more obvious than the lady with goat legs, who can only hide them by wearing a floor length short skirt and hoping you don't notice the clip-clop of hooves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, and there's the part where the Lunars are the only part of the game line where there's a <i>set difficulty</i> to notice those kinds of details on a non-quick character. I presume that if Mara wanted to hide her goat legs, she'd be rolling Intelligence + Larceny, just like any other disguise attempt (though probably with a penalty). But as written, no Lunar can even attempt to do better at disguising the Tell than the flat Perception difficulty given for it, regardless of any and all other factors that go into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","user":"Roadie","date":". 02-20-2019, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:13:29-08:00","id":1289826,"title":"","content":"It could be kind of a patch for having Lunar protagonists or antagonists? Like the PC version of the Tell is with SSD, where as antagonist Lunars might tend not to have it unless they're particularly adept at it. I forsee a lot of players just considering it a kind of tax, unless they really don't use shapeshifting for stealth at all, and a lot of STs just giving it to every single Lunar and making the Tell kind of pointless for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:24:03-08:00","id":1289827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289825#post1289825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, and there's the part where the Lunars are the only part of the game line where there's a <i>set difficulty</i> to notice those kinds of details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in most cases, &quot;that person has cat ears&quot; is not the kind of detail that you require any kind of roll to make at all.<br /> <br /> The set difficulty is an obstacle, not an invitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that if Mara wanted to hide her goat legs, she'd be rolling Intelligence + Larceny, just like any other disguise attempt (though probably with a penalty).</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose so. Mara's deer legs are tragically not gifted with innate magic that will conceal them from all but the most puissant senses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as written, no Lunar can even attempt to do better at disguising the Tell than the flat Perception difficulty given for it, regardless of any and all other factors that go into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, on the one hand... orichalcum rule. I don't think it's a huge stretch to assume that if a Lunar's Tell is their little goat horns, and they spend all of their time wearing a hat, then the Tell doesn't really get an opportunity to present itself. It's not like Second Edition, where the rules are telling you where you can and cannot put the Tell. Depending on circumstances, never taking your hat off might be a bit suspicious, though.<br /> <br /> I mean, for the sake of its dramatic potential, I see no point in being somebody whose Tell is placed on a part of their body where a roll to perceive it would never make sense. But assuming that it could be noticed sans disguise or other concealment (like staying out of bright lights so nobody sees your weird shadow), I don't think a bit of mundane concealment is out of order, if sometimes inconveniencing.<br /> <br /> Although I still think that a flaring anima will illustrate its form and presence.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you seem to be being really evasive about just how high that difficulty is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:30:07-08:00","id":1289828,"title":"","content":"Let me simplify it even more: the Tell is a thing because the Wyld Hunt needs to stand a chance.<br /> <br /> With a difficulty of 7, a mortal spotting a Tell, or even an Exalted who has no reason to suspect you spotting it by luck, are virtually impossible. But Exalted characters actively on the look out for a given Lunar need some degree to which they stand a chance to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T01:30:20-08:00","id":1289845,"title":"","content":"Huh, and I had the opposite reaction, the Tell is such a cool and evocative thing to me that I winced when I found that Subtle Silver Declaration was still in the game. I'm more concerned about it blocking access to charms I might actually want than feeling as though it's a tax. But then in the old days it seemed forumites considered the way I played a Lunar 'wrong' and I struggle to recognise the Exalted other people play as the same game as mine sometimes, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T04:15:51-08:00","id":1289865,"title":"","content":"I mean, in 3e you can also take a mutation to represent your tell, which is obvious (although the fact that it's a tell isn't) and persists between forms. That might be an issue when disguising yourself as a human. But there's also Moon's Hidden Face, which can make mutations subtle, and in this case I guess would make the tell switch to working like a normal one. <br /> <br /> Point is, Lunars are potentially masters of disguise, but they need to put in <i>some</i> effort. It's possible to be good at hiding <i>by lunar standards. </i>Which I think makes it more meaningful as a character concept. It gives Changing Moons a better purchase on their identity. They are not just &quot;the other guys&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:25:09-08:00","id":1289871,"title":"","content":"Basically, Lunars having a consistent feature based on their totem is both a) mythology-based and b) cool.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I'm not keen on forcing characters into stuff, but at the same time characters require theme.<br /> <br /> I find that with pretty much every Lunar I've played with, I liked their Tell.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, admittedly, it was mechanically borked, but they've cleaned it up this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:52:13-08:00","id":1289879,"title":"","content":"Actually, speaking of forcing characters into stuff, it seems like the Tell is in some ways a lot less restrictive than a caste mark. Sure, it's 'on' all the time but at least as a player you get to decide what it is (even if I sometimes feel mine was a little iffy), whereas there's no option with a caste mark even if it is mostly 'off'.<br /> Why does my Dawn caste have to have a daft sun picture on his forehead when he flares and not, like, the Old Realm for 'Justice' or 'Honour', or my Full Moon weep glowing tears of silver essence rather than have a flat silver disc sit on his brow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:52:56-08:00","id":1289880,"title":"","content":"We're about 30 session XP past chargen in our new Chronicle, and our DBs and Solars both hit difficulty 7 routinely on any roll they're built to undertake and spend Essence on. <br /> <br /> About a quarter of that difficulty ( 2 / 7 ) is already reached with a really good stunt, if their WP is full. The remaining 5 are expected on a roll of 10 dice. <br /> <br /> <br /> What if, hypothetically, the difficulty to spot the Tell had a stuntable bonus, if your Lunar has a good description of their actions?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:12:47-08:00","id":1289912,"title":"","content":"I don't know about a stunt for the Tell, but I'd impose a penalty to the roll if, say, the Lunar is hiding their wolf ears under a hat. But also, you know, maybe a demigod whose legend is that they are supernaturally perceptive should have a good chance of spotting Lunars. I don't think it's a problem if exalts who have focused in that area are a problem for Lunars. It'd be cheesy as hell if the ST kept giving every antagonist 14 dice on their &quot;spot Lunars&quot; dice pool, but one or two, especially recurring antagonists and nemeses, sounds like fair play. Coming at it from the other end, if you want to have challenging, sneaky Lunar adversaries for your circle or hearth, there are Charms for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:57:49-08:00","id":1289925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289880#post1289880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're about 30 session XP past chargen in our new Chronicle, and our DBs and Solars both hit difficulty 7 routinely on any roll they're built to undertake and spend Essence on.<br /> <br /> About a quarter of that difficulty ( 2 / 7 ) is already reached with a really good stunt, if their WP is full. The remaining 5 are expected on a roll of 10 dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if, hypothetically, the difficulty to spot the Tell had a stuntable bonus, if your Lunar has a good description of their actions?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So... your solars and DB do things that the majority of creation would find impossible? Are you saying that this is <i>not</i> working as intended?<br /> <br /> Attribute 5, ability 5 is essentially exclusive to PCs and majorly high-level antagonists. like 99.999% of the rest of the population have no chance to ever hit 7 difficulty.<br /> <br /> Plus, if your Characters are doing a level 2 stunt and spending a WP on a Perception roll... I'm pretty sure they already know that there's a lunar there, they're just double checking. It's utterly ludicrous to assume that <i>everybody</i> is going to that level of bother just in case there might be a lunar around that they've seen the tell of.<br /> <br /> Edit: For clarity I'm assuming a level 2 stunt because otherwise you'd blow through your willpower pool about 10 min into a session if you spend one on <i>every roll.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:18:16-08:00","id":1289933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289880#post1289880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're about 30 session XP past chargen in our new Chronicle, and our DBs and Solars both hit difficulty 7 routinely on any roll they're built to undertake and spend Essence on.<br /> <br /> About a quarter of that difficulty ( 2 / 7 ) is already reached with a really good stunt, if their WP is full. The remaining 5 are expected on a roll of 10 dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if, hypothetically, the difficulty to spot the Tell had a stuntable bonus, if your Lunar has a good description of their actions?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do your party members regularly spend Essence to check people they meet for Lunar Tells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:59:08-08:00","id":1289954,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I think with perception you're supposed to be able to spend essence passively without your character actively looking for something. It's modelling you being hyper alert and shit.<br /> <br /> That said, I also don't think a lunar who has no investment whatsoever in hiding their nature getting found out is anything but the system working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:36:59-08:00","id":1289972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again#post1289791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience with previous editions, the Tell mechanic has always been at best kind of annoying. This one looks poised to repeat that: it's got the same fiddly thing going on where high enough rolls can see through it regardless of shape, until a minor investment then negates it entirely most of the time. In practice, this just makes the Charm to hide an obligatory tax for characters that ever plan to do social infiltration stuff, while others just won't care most of the time. On top of that, the GM will be stuck keeping track of who has or hasn't seen through it for individual PCs whenever recurring NPCs come up.<br /> <br /> Like, what's the reason to even include it? What do the game and its themes actually gain in play from forcing characters to have a distinctive quality that, broadly speaking, either they'll immediately suppress from character creation or they'll never care about enough to interact with mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>The base Tell so far is P+A difficulty 7, for nontrivial characters. Think about that for a moment. First of all, it walls off discovery from random npcs, so you know the only people who you're vulnerable to people who would have mattered to the story in the first place. Secondly, Difficulty 7 is about right, in my opinion, as it requires either four 10s, a success on all seven die, or most likely Awareness Charms to trigger. True, a lot of people seem to dump into Awareness anyway due to Join Battle rolls (unless you're a Stealth-Supremo or Tiger-Warrior-Resistance Solar (based on personal experience)), but seven dice still means your opponent is above average in either Perception or Awareness ++++ cresting the mountain of physical training and form in the other, so your opponent is a true rival worthy of having their heart eaten. Third, the fact that difficulty diminishes by 1 for people who know you means it's either a friend you put time and effort into cultivating, or an intense rival / foe you also put gametime and effort cultivating..... that sounds awesome. Finally, the bonfire flare making it obvious? C'mon. You're already visible for miles. Your Tell is the last thing you should be concerned about there. You also gain back 5 motes a round in combat, so you almost have to Bonfire On Purpose to trigger it (have had a Solar game where nobody's even bonfired once, 12+ sessions in.... and a Dragonblooded game where the players consistently bonfire On Purpose).<br /> <br /> This Tell mechanic seems reasonable.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:39:42-08:00","id":1289974,"title":"","content":"To generally answer the replies above...<br /> <br /> The scaling of my players' characters' rolls assumes:<br /> <br /> It's something they're good at. With 4 or 5 characters, depending on who shows up, there aren't a lot of Abilities that aren't covered by somebody. Which is definitely as-intended. The characters who'd be covering that Ability typically have Attributes to match, so a natural dice pool of 8 to 10 is not abnormal. Plus specialty.<br /> <br /> It's something they're interested in. I didn't separate out a perception roll in mentioning it, so that applies to fighting, crafting, socializing, shaping sorcery, and so on... any task they'd engage in and use Excellency/Charms/Stunts into. I don't typically call for perception rolls (in Exalted) if there's nothing to find. So, it's natural that they'd take an interest and follow through with their best.<br /> <br /> Each character is making their roll separately. Some tasks are only done by one character, and sometimes that's keeping watch. I do make sure characters who are doing something else aren't the ones making perception rolls for instance, but if the whole Circle is searching or otherwise ready and free to act, they'd all get a chance to spot. The odds of everybody in a Circle failing to roll a 7 start vanishing rapidly as the size of the Circle grows.<br /> <br /> [Edit to add here] A roll like a perception roll tends to stand for a Scene unless something changes. I don't make players roll over and over every time some random townie walks around the corner. So, I don't disincentivize characters spending some Essence on that roll. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, yes, 7 is a really easy target number if someone is good at that task, engages with that task, and has a cue that it's time to do that task.<br /> <br /> <br /> Worth mentioning as an aside - I do make use of nothing-there perception rolls in other game settings. D&amp;D or WoD/CoD can both benefit from those, just to bring the creepy/creaky/crawly theme to the story. I also sometimes ask for declarations and make secret rolls in other settings. They don't seem to fit the themes I'd usually bring to Exalted, because I want the players to be in control of the excellency of their Chosen. Your motes may vary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:55:56-08:00","id":1289981,"title":"","content":"It's probably a fair point that when you make 5 players roll Perception+Awareness, 1 of them's probably going to get 7 successes, even if most don't.<br /> <br /> Which again, is fine. We're talking about a group of the most powerful people in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:43:56-08:00","id":1290005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289981#post1289981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably a fair point that when you make 5 players roll Perception+Awareness, 1 of them's probably going to get 7 successes, even if most don't.<br /> <br /> Which again, is fine. We're talking about a group of the most powerful people in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with that it would still take effort via charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:52:51-08:00","id":1290010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289974#post1289974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To generally answer the replies above...<br /> <br /> The scaling of my players' characters' rolls assumes:<br /> <br /> It's something they're good at. With 4 or 5 characters, depending on who shows up, there aren't a lot of Abilities that aren't covered by somebody. Which is definitely as-intended. The characters who'd be covering that Ability typically have Attributes to match, so a natural dice pool of 8 to 10 is not abnormal. Plus specialty.<br /> <br /> It's something they're interested in. I didn't separate out a perception roll in mentioning it, so that applies to fighting, crafting, socializing, shaping sorcery, and so on... any task they'd engage in and use Excellency/Charms/Stunts into. I don't typically call for perception rolls (in Exalted) if there's nothing to find. So, it's natural that they'd take an interest and follow through with their best.<br /> <br /> Each character is making their roll separately. Some tasks are only done by one character, and sometimes that's keeping watch. I do make sure characters who are doing something else aren't the ones making perception rolls for instance, but if the whole Circle is searching or otherwise ready and free to act, they'd all get a chance to spot. The odds of everybody in a Circle failing to roll a 7 start vanishing rapidly as the size of the Circle grows.<br /> <br /> [Edit to add here] A roll like a perception roll tends to stand for a Scene unless something changes. I don't make players roll over and over every time some random townie walks around the corner. So, I don't disincentivize characters spending some Essence on that roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, yes, 7 is a really easy target number if <i><b>AN EXALT PC</b></i> is good at that task, engages with that task, and has a cue that it's time to do that task.<br /> <br /> <br /> Worth mentioning as an aside - I do make use of nothing-there perception rolls in other game settings. D&amp;D or WoD/CoD can both benefit from those, just to bring the creepy/creaky/crawly theme to the story. I also sometimes ask for declarations and make secret rolls in other settings. They don't seem to fit the themes I'd usually bring to Exalted, because I want the players to be in control of the excellency of their Chosen. Your motes may vary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:05:39-08:00","id":1290047,"title":"","content":"Looking at it from a wider perspective, I think it\u2019s a good thing. Lunars, especially this edition, are not defined by their ability to shapeshift. You can easily be an ungodly powerful and versatile Lunar and never change shape at all. I think that\u2019s been proven by the charms we\u2019ve seen so far. <br /> <br /> Imperfect shapeshifting is just like a bonus on top of that, like dragonblooded anima damage except waaaaaay better. It SHOULD require charms to make that shapeshifting into a perfect disguise or allow transformation into Tyrant Lizards. And, as pointed out, unless the Lunar is trying to fool PCs or sneak into the Mask of Winters personal study the 7 difficulty is well above anyone\u2019s ability to get.<br /> <br /> Like a normal DB who is quite good at spotting things with percep 3 and awareness 3, with a full excellency they\u2019ve still got a really low chance of making it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:51:29-08:00","id":1290058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290047#post1290047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imperfect shapeshifting is just like a bonus on top of that, like dragonblooded anima damage except waaaaaay better. It SHOULD require charms to make that shapeshifting into a perfect disguise or allow transformation into Tyrant Lizards. And, as pointed out, unless the Lunar is trying to fool PCs or sneak into the Mask of Winters personal study the 7 difficulty is well above anyone\u2019s ability to get.<br /> <br /> Like a normal DB who is quite good at spotting things with percep 3 and awareness 3, with a full excellency they\u2019ve still got a really low chance of making it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. If I want to make a character who defined as a face-stealing infiltrator, I can't meaningfully claim that role in my circle if the other characters can easily do it to without charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:31:43-08:00","id":1290082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again#post1289791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, this just makes the Charm to hide an obligatory tax for characters that ever plan to do social infiltration stuff, while others just won't care most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's explicitly it's purpose, and a very fair one<br /> <br /> Lunar shapeshifting with no tell would mean that a chargen lunar with zero experience invested would be the equivalent of Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise + Perfect Mirror + Flashing Ruse Prana + a theoreticle fourth solar larceny charm that let's you disguise as animals. And this is on top of the insane other bonuses you can get with shapeshifting. This is something every lunar can do, having it be flight for whoever wants it, breathing underwater for whoever wants it, a pseudo infinite ability mastery in combat for non maxed combat builds, and in general everything else shapeshifting let's you do, all for no cost is a pretty big balance issue. So here, and in a few other places like the charms necessary for legendary size for instance, the game asks &quot;hey can you buy at least like one charm to be as good as the entire solar disguise tree?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:33:03-08:00","id":1290084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290010#post1290010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixed that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything I posted was broken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd only let a mortal have a chance to catch on to a player's Lunar if something has <i>Gone Very Wrong</i> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(tm)</span> . <br /> <br /> It's the Exalted and their peers who would be the ones who would roll. That means PC's trying to catch NPC Lunars, and NPC Exalted and peers trying to catch PC Lunars. <br /> <br /> In the case of NPCs trying to catch PC Lunars, I'd probably have it happen in the context of one or more challenges along the way to their goal. Maybe they're crossing a no-man's land during a battle, or infiltrating a Manse, for example. In those situations, it seems reasonable and dramatic that the NPCs would be alert and cued to use (at least) their Reflexive Charms to spot something out of the ordinary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:12:39-08:00","id":1290115,"title":"","content":"I can kind of see the attitude, partly because in a lot of ways 2e Lunars were just Solars except the crappy versions with weaker powers and more restrictions, except for shapeshifting. Shapeshifting was like the one thing you got to lord over the Solars in the group, so it can kind of feel like the Lunars were just the Shapeshifters who could also do some other stuff okay too. Like regeneration, that's a thing they're alright at.<br /> <br /> Now, however, this is not the case. Invincible Beast-Warrior Empowerment alone is powerful beyond anything in the Solar war tree. Part of that is because the Solar war tree focuses a lot more on strategic warfare, but even considering that I don't see much that matches it. Lunars no longer need to rely on shapeshifting to set them apart and be powerful, they just already are the badasses of the world right now.<br /> <br /> Going through the Lunar charms as I have been doing is actually kind of making shapeshifting seem like too much. It isn't of course, but like you read through 3 charms and go &quot;Wow, and then you can combo these together and...holy crap.&quot; then on top of that you get all the benefits of base shapeshifting? If it wasn't for Supernals you'd wonder why anyone would even want to play a Solar anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:29:08-08:00","id":1290134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290115#post1290115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invincible Beast-Warrior Empowerment alone is powerful beyond anything in the Solar war tree. Part of that is because the Solar war tree focuses a lot more on strategic warfare</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, I think the biggest part of it is that we don't actually have a published Solar War Charm at Essence 4 yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:32:04-08:00","id":1290135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290134#post1290134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fairness, I think the biggest part of it is that we don't actually have a published Solar War Charm at Essence 4 yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also 100% there is bias on my part because I'm going through a new charm set foaming at the mouth like a Last Airbender background character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:49:36-08:00","id":1290156,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a specific note in the section on the Tell that says \u201ccircumstances may impose penalties on rolls to notice a Lunar\u2019s Tell.\u201d I would include \u201cwearing a hat over it,\u201d \u201chiding it with makeup,\u201d \u201cwearing dark glasses,\u201d \u201chiding it under a hairband,\u201d and similar methods to all count for \u201ccircumstantial penalties\u201d<br /> <br /> So, a Lunar can work hard to disguise their Tell even without a charm. They just can\u2019t make it invisible without a charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:14:20-08:00","id":1290169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1289845#post1289845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, and I had the opposite reaction, the Tell is such a cool and evocative thing to me that I winced when I found that Subtle Silver Declaration was still in the game. I'm more concerned about it blocking access to charms I might actually want than feeling as though it's a tax. But then in the old days it seemed forumites considered the way I played a Lunar 'wrong' and I struggle to recognise the Exalted other people play as the same game as mine sometimes, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the problem I have here is that the Tell has never felt even the least bit &quot;cool&quot; to me. I've never come across a Tell that, given the mechanics for it, didn't come across as either bad-Photoshop ridiculous (&quot;songbird with a leopard's tail or ram's horns&quot;) or like bad-anime-OC exaggerated speshul distinctive features in a way that gets even sillier once you have a group of Lunars together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290047#post1290047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imperfect shapeshifting is just like a bonus on top of that, like dragonblooded anima damage except waaaaaay better. It SHOULD require charms to make that shapeshifting into a perfect disguise or allow transformation into Tyrant Lizards. And, as pointed out, unless the Lunar is trying to fool PCs or sneak into the Mask of Winters personal study the 7 difficulty is well above anyone\u2019s ability to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would be fine with that! I would actually find it really cool if Lunars had to actively do something to build up their stronger forms out of mutation points, put some investment into disguise attempts and Survival to not instantly stick out with inaccurate animal behavior, <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/BFNnSSU.png\" target=\"_blank\">had to practice with specific forms to avoid being subtly 'off' in ways that raise peoples' hackles</a>, or whatever. But I think that &quot;all forms share a single blatant trait, except also it tries to hide itself??&quot; is a <i>really awful</i> way to accomplish that, and I don't understand why it's just been carried across as-is for multiple editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290156#post1290156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a specific note in the section on the Tell that says \u201ccircumstances may impose penalties on rolls to notice a Lunar\u2019s Tell.\u201d I would include \u201cwearing a hat over it,\u201d \u201chiding it with makeup,\u201d \u201cwearing dark glasses,\u201d \u201chiding it under a hairband,\u201d and similar methods to all count for \u201ccircumstantial penalties\u201d<br /> <br /> So, a Lunar can work hard to disguise their Tell even without a charm. They just can\u2019t make it invisible without a charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally feel that mechanical notes that amount to &quot;and the GM can do whatever&quot; are actively worse than useless. The GM can <i>always </i>do whatever, that's why there's a GM in the first place! If text like that is going to exist, it should actually interact with existing rules, like the ones for rolling disguises, instead of just being a vague shrug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","user":"Roadie","date":". 02-20-2019, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T20:46:34-08:00","id":1290229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290169#post1290169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think that &quot;all forms share a single blatant trait, except also it tries to hide itself??&quot; is a <i>really awful</i> way to accomplish that, and I don't understand why it's just been carried across as-is for multiple editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in this edition it actually isn't necessarily blatant, it could be very subtle. The songbird voice or the moving shadow, or even the blind eye or scare don't scream Lunar in particular, and could be really hard to spot if you're not looking for them. The scar and the eye don't even hint at anything supernatural at all. It just has to be something that you could theoretically notice. It DOES supernaturally hide itself though, it's like a psyche effect that pressures your mind into not noticing it.<br /> <br /> There are reasons to do it that way though, instead of just making it actually something barely noticeable like an imperceptible wrong-ness about them or something. One is that the Tell not only ousts you as a Lunar, but as a specific Lunar. To do that the Tell has to be different for everyone, and at that point the only really fair way to do it is to let the Lunar pick what's up with their disguises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290169#post1290169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally feel that mechanical notes that amount to &quot;and the GM can do whatever&quot; are actively worse than useless. The GM can <i>always </i>do whatever, that's why there's a GM in the first place! If text like that is going to exist, it should actually interact with existing rules, like the ones for rolling disguises, instead of just being a vague shrug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that happens a lot in Exalted. Like there's a ton of DB charms that stop &quot;environmental penalties&quot; but there's basically zero official environmental penalties, just page 188 of the corebook that sets out some suggestions. Usually from 1-5 dice somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T03:46:01-08:00","id":1290289,"title":"","content":"Frankly I think giving a lunar yu-gi-oh tier anime hair that nobody notices sounds absolutely hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:25:18-08:00","id":1290359,"title":"","content":"On top of all this, te Tell's not even a dead giveaway for lunar. Plenty people and creatures have such quirks when you start dealing with the supernatural that the Tell's only telling you that the subject is not normal.<br /> So, in practice, a Lunar that doesn't go out of her way to hide the Tell's not at risk of being <i>identified</i>, unless it's a recurring event with a recurring character that is resourceful enough to find that connection.<br /> <br /> By that point you're either going balls to the wall overt or you have a bloodhound after you.<br /> Looks pretty fine to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:20:31-08:00","id":1290442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290359#post1290359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of all this, te Tell's not even a dead giveaway for lunar. Plenty people and creatures have such quirks when you start dealing with the supernatural that the Tell's only telling you that the subject is not normal.<br /> So, in practice, a Lunar that doesn't go out of her way to hide the Tell's not at risk of being <i>identified</i>, unless it's a recurring event with a recurring character that is resourceful enough to find that connection.<br /> <br /> By that point you're either going balls to the wall overt or you have a bloodhound after you.<br /> Looks pretty fine to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when you think about the little cosmetic effects that certain control spells have on the sorcerer; even if it your Tell is something unnatural, like a wandering shadow, plenty of people might just go &quot;oh crap, sorcerer&quot; which is definitely better than &quot;ANATHEMA! RUN!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:05:45-08:00","id":1290503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290169#post1290169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never come across a Tell that, given the mechanics for it, didn't come across as either bad-Photoshop ridiculous (&quot;songbird with a leopard's tail or ram's horns&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics have always, always, always said that features like that are adjusted into something that is fitting for the alternative shape. Your songbird has the tail of a songbird, which might be unusually speckled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually find it really cool if Lunars had to actively do something to build up their stronger forms out of mutation points, put some investment into disguise attempts and Survival to not instantly stick out with inaccurate animal behavior, <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/BFNnSSU.png\" target=\"_blank\">had to practice with specific forms to avoid being subtly 'off' in ways that raise peoples' hackles</a>, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that you want the Lunars as a baseline to be distinctly bad at their essential, iconic capability?<br /> <br /> Never mind that, on this occasion, a Lunar making a really bad job of acting in-character has explicitly been made a basis for observers to get decent bonuses to their rolls to see through them. That is more than they got in Second Edition; in Second Edition, a person had to be specifically on the lookout for Lunars or shapeshifters, for which they might get as many as a whole <i>two</i> points to their Mental Defence Value.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, that was another thing about how it worked; you didn't roll for observation against a flat penalty, the Tell was treated as a social attack with a flat value of 12 successes, meaning that anybody with up to a Mental Defence Value of <i>eleven</i> straight up couldn't see it. If you had prior familiarity with what a given Lunar's Tell was, and were specifically on the lookout for Lunars, you generously only needed to have a Mental Defence Value of <b>8</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why it's just been carried across as-is for multiple editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one thing, there's the literary background that every single respondent has referred to, to which you've replied nothing. Then there's the fact that describing it as being carried along as-is is not accurate, as the mechanical implementation goes. As I understand it, First Edition didn't model the question of seeing the Tell and making the connection at all, and Second Edition used the system I described above, in which the requirements are fairly high, there's not really any direct action on anybody's part, and nothing comes from how the Lunar acts.<br /> <br /> Here you have a system in which the integrity of a Lunar's most basic magical disguise is something that can be severely compromised by such things as having openly been a Lunar in a different form in front of the observer in the past, making a poor job of playing who or what you're pretending to be, and being up against somebody canny and observant enough to read your intentions or profile you and realise that you're probably not who you say you are.<br /> <br /> The Tell as it currently is has some back and forth, affords more dynamic agency to an observer, and can actually add a bit of tension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally feel that mechanical notes that amount to &quot;and the GM can do whatever&quot; are actively worse than useless. The GM can <i>always </i>do whatever, that's why there's a GM in the first place! If text like that is going to exist, it should actually interact with existing rules, like the ones for rolling disguises, instead of just being a vague shrug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to the manner in which it gives guidelines for ways in which characters can get extra dice to see through the disguise?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:08:21-08:00","id":1290570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290134#post1290134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fairness, I think the biggest part of it is that we don't actually have a published Solar War Charm at Essence 4 yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if we were to go back to 1e's Craft (War) to hijack one of the many 3e Craft Charms and oh my it seems that my brain is trying to leak out through my nose just from thinking about Craft (War) as a conceptual detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:08:21-08:00","id":1290571,"title":"","content":"At least 10 characters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":".  Mouse made accidental double-tap on post. 02-21-2019, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:16:17-08:00","id":1290577,"title":"","content":"I don't get it.<br /> <br /> (Wouldn't Craft (War) just be building siege engines and fortifications and stuff?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:04:32-08:00","id":1291602,"title":"","content":"I find it kind of telling (heh) that the art for Tula uses the cop-out of (presumably) the scar as a Tell. Like, that's been a &quot;man, I don't even know, just do whatever&quot; cliche for Lunars for years and years, and even the developers are doing it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290503#post1290503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics have always, always, always said that features like that are adjusted into something that is fitting for the alternative shape. Your songbird has the tail of a songbird, which might be unusually speckled.</div> </div> </div> </div>...which makes the &quot;recognize as the same individual&quot; mechanic even sillier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290503#post1290503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying that you want the Lunars as a baseline to be distinctly bad at their essential, iconic capability?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290503#post1290503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tell as it currently is has some back and forth, affords more dynamic agency to an observer, and can actually add a bit of tension.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's really a desperate need for Lunars to have some kind of give-away with their shapechanging, I would rather have them be &quot;bad at it&quot; in in a way that feels natural and requires some investment to be good at it, and actually interacts with other systems in the game like disguises and noticing disguises, rather than have what's implicitly described as perfect shifting but then drop on a trait that only exists to be a downside in the character creation chapter with entirely standalone mechanics that just kind of waggle fingers vaguely at the GM to reinvent disguise rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290503#post1290503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for one thing, there's the literary background that every single respondent has referred to, to which you've replied nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are mythical shapechangers that have giveaway traits. Why must there be an obsessive focus on those ones, who are almost always antagonists, not protagonists, over mythical and literary sources where there are shapechanging protagonists that don't? Why make it <i>mandatory</i> for PCs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290577#post1290577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it.<br /> <br /> (Wouldn't Craft (War) just be building siege engines and fortifications and stuff?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, see, Craft (War) would be what Conrad Brean does in <i>Wag the Dog</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:43:42-08:00","id":1291619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291602#post1291602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there are mythical shapechangers that have giveaway traits. Why must there be an obsessive focus on those ones, who are almost always antagonists, not protagonists, over mythical and literary sources where there are shapechanging protagonists that don't? Why make it <i>mandatory</i> for PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Lunars <i>are</i> those shapeshifters. Their whole deal is that they are monstrous heroes and guardian devils. A typical Lunar protagonist is indeed the villain of a typical Dynast's story.<br /> <br /> And because, frankly, the perfect kind of shapeshifter sounds really freaking boring to play. There's a reason a common Mary Sue Power is &quot;shapeshifting without true limits or downsides.&quot; It's not a power anyone can reasonably counter, which leads to the problem of making the Silver Pact seem stronger than their nemeses, the Realm, as opposed to equally powerful or slightly weaker. That brings down both of them (it makes the Scarlet Empire, masters of All Creation, seem like a stronger-than-average rainstorm away from collapsing, and it undersells how cunning, strong and <i>heroic </i>the Silver Pact is for having become its collective nightmare).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-24-2019, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:45:55-08:00","id":1291635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1290577#post1290577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it.<br /> <br /> (Wouldn't Craft (War) just be building siege engines and fortifications and stuff?)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one part of it, but it also explicitly covered formation placement and logistics, among other details of armed conflict. 1e was a strange time, where Performance covered mass combat and training of troops, even though Presence was explicitly supposed to have those roles in its description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T17:21:43-08:00","id":1291659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291602#post1291602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it kind of telling (heh) that the art for Tula uses the cop-out of (presumably) the scar as a Tell. Like, that's been a &quot;man, I don't even know, just do whatever&quot; cliche for Lunars for years and years, and even the developers are doing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez, here I was thinking that knowing that's No Moon because you've seen that scar before on a different face could be an effectively compelling turnaround.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which makes the &quot;recognize as the same individual&quot; mechanic even sillier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know an answer like this indicates that there's really no winning, because every response will just feed into another complaint, but I just want to do something to kind of close the circle a bit.<br /> <br /> I feel as though a game such as Exalted is, not unreasonably, asking for a decent amount of dramatic license. I'm not talking about in the stuff like the existence of gods and millenia-old demigods (although it is in some of the implications of their existence, such as not trying to be too deep about the question of what a person who has lived for thousands of years might logically be expected to be like), but in some of the things such as how the history has unfolded, how personalities clash against each other, some of the ways that institutions in the world can work and, most pertinent to this discussion, ways in which the mechanics prioritise making dynamic and engaging stories rather than being an arms race.<br /> <br /> Hence you get stunting, mechanical rewards just for describing things happening in interesting ways. Hence the description of the basic mechanical difficulties, from how the lowest difficulty sets the baseline of &quot;stuff heroes do all the time&quot; (indicating that this isn't stuff for everyday life), up to difficulty 5, in which people can do kind of impossible stuff like read print by feel.<br /> <br /> And here we're talking about an action that is difficulty 7.<br /> <br /> So is it strictly logical that a person might make the leap that the speckles on the tail of that bird look distinctly out of place, or (probably more likely) find recognition in them from what they've seen on a Lunar in the past? Well... honestly probably a little more likely than one would think, people have done stranger things. But the important thing is that it creates a dramatic avenue for a Lunar being sussed out. Not an unearned one, mind, not a convenient one. Even if you have seen the Tell before, open and exposed by the light of the anima banner, you're going down from &quot;basically only gods could notice this&quot; to &quot;some of the most heroic observational types in the world would have to strain to see this (and draw the important connections) even before it being one of their bad days&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's really a desperate need for Lunars to have some kind of give-away with their shapechanging, I would rather have them be &quot;bad at it&quot; in in a way that feels natural and requires some investment to be good at it<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, and actually interacts with other systems in the game like disguises and noticing disguises</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>And a lot of people would probably argue really vehemently against it.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting for Lunars is, after all, more than just a feature, it's supposed to be a bit of a selling point. Sprucing it up a bit over mere disguises could be viewed as part of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">rather than have what's implicitly described as perfect shifting but then drop on a trait that only exists to be a downside in the character creation chapter with entirely standalone mechanics that just kind of waggle fingers vaguely at the GM to reinvent disguise rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this is really not giving fair shakes to what the book describes and affords for seeing through the deception. As in, rather than being focused on the disguise rules, it places most of the heft on the read intentions and profile character rules. If anything, the fact that the best first step to seeing through it is not in the body, but recognising something off in the underlying personality, kind of reinforces that the shifting is paradoxically perfect in spite of its giveaway feature.<br /> <br /> (Implicit descriptions are great, aren't they? They let people project whatever meaning to the text that allows them to be outraged at it being contrary to what is explicit.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there are mythical shapechangers that have giveaway traits. Why must there be an obsessive focus on those ones, who are almost always antagonists, not protagonists, over mythical and literary sources where there are shapechanging protagonists that don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Leliel already gave a good answer for this, and... that is all I need to say about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make it <i>mandatory</i> for PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from all of the dramatic reasons, so that the selling point of shapeshifting doesn't also turn into something that basically saps tension altogether out of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T17:30:20-08:00","id":1291661,"title":"","content":"The tell also lets you carry a mutation between all of your forms. <br /> <br /> Say hello to Mr I-Always-Have-Wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T17:45:23-08:00","id":1291664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291661#post1291661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tell also lets you carry a mutation between all of your forms.<br /> <br /> Say hello to Mr I-Always-Have-Wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That seems a bit broken? Is there a merit or charm I am missing? What stops people from picking a huge slew of mutations for their tell?<br /> <br /> *Ok I re-read the rules I apparently missed. I feel like if your tell is something like giant wings it should be harder to hide because that is extremely obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 02-24-2019, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:14:47-08:00","id":1291673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291664#post1291664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? That seems a bit broken? Is there a merit or charm I am missing? What stops people from picking a huge slew of mutations for their tell?<br /> <br /> *Ok I re-read the rules I apparently missed. I feel like if your tell is something like giant wings it should be harder to hide because that is extremely obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Query, Subtle Silver Declaration, does it hide the mutation the Tell is attached to or the fact that it is a Lunar tell?<br /> <br /> Or is that too fine a hair to split and everything is hidden? (I\u2019m only asking here and not in ask the devs as it might have already been answered.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:18:19-08:00","id":1291674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291659#post1291659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez, here I was thinking that knowing that's No Moon because you've seen that scar before on a different face could be an effectively compelling turnaround.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be blunt: &quot;I recognize that scar!&quot; as a plot point in a story would almost certainly just make me shake my head and stop reading because it was too dumb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291659#post1291659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting for Lunars is, after all, more than just a feature, it's supposed to be a bit of a selling point. Sprucing it up a bit over mere disguises could be viewed as part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Tell basically is a built-in disguise, just with a set difficulty. Of course, by not actually being stated as such it's left to the GM to haphazardly rule on its interactions with any Perception or Awareness Charms that interact with disguises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291659#post1291659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though this is really not giving fair shakes to what the book describes and affords for seeing through the deception. As in, rather than being focused on the disguise rules, it places most of the heft on the read intentions and profile character rules. If anything, the fact that the best first step to seeing through it is not in the body, but recognising something off in the underlying personality, kind of reinforces that the shifting is paradoxically perfect in spite of its giveaway feature.<br /> <br /> (Implicit descriptions are great, aren't they? They let people project whatever meaning to the text that allows them to be outraged at it being contrary to what is explicit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most of the heft&quot; is overselling literally half a sentence out of four paragraphs, and half of a sentence that doesn't even give concrete mechanics.<br /> <br /> I think part of the fundamental problem here for me is the text is trying to tie every way to notice a Lunar is out of place to this one mechanic about a physical trait, instead of any kind of more broad rules or guidelines on fitting into the role, whether or not perfect shapechanging is involved. It's like an extended repeat of how entire rules systems in the Ex3 core book don't actually exist and have to be inferred backwards out of the character mechanics instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291659#post1291659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from all of the dramatic reasons, so that the selling point of shapeshifting doesn't also turn into something that basically saps tension altogether out of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why does Subtle Silver Declaration exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:25:14-08:00","id":1291676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be blunt: &quot;I recognize that scar!&quot; as a plot point in a story would almost certainly just make me shake my head and stop reading because it was too dumb. </div> </div> </div>You not liking the type of stories Lunars are based on is a personal taste issue, not a failing on the part of the Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then why does Subtle Silver Declaration exist? </div> </div> </div>SSD is only renders the Tell absolutely unnoticable to people who have never seen it before. Lunars don't have an absolute defense against being noticed by a recurring Wyld Hunt nemesis on their heels, NOR SHOULD THEY BECAUSE THAT'S IMPORTANT STORY FODDER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:39:10-08:00","id":1291677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291676#post1291676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You not liking the type of stories Lunars are based on is a personal taste issue, not a failing on the part of the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really trying to claim this for the <i>scar</i> example, when that's been the &quot;I couldn't think of a good Tell so I guess I'll just make it a scar&quot; anti-use of the mechanic since the 2e days?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291676#post1291676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SSD is only renders the Tell absolutely unnoticable to people who have never seen it before. Lunars don't have an absolute defense against being noticed by a recurring Wyld Hunt nemesis on their heels, NOR SHOULD THEY BECAUSE THAT'S IMPORTANT STORY FODDER.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules for tracking and recognizing supernatural shapechangers would be a good thing, but none of that necessitates the need for a Lunar-only mechanic that exists entirely to be a single negative trait slapped onto otherwise perfect shapechanging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291673#post1291673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query, Subtle Silver Declaration, does it hide the mutation the Tell is attached to or the fact that it is a Lunar tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>My read is that it doesn't hide the mutation, but it does turn off the &quot;anyone who succeeds against the difficulty automatically knows it's you&quot; effect, at which point the game just shrugs and makes your GM figure out by themselves how to deal with characters possibly not-automatically figuring out that the dog with gills and the eagle with gills are same shapechanger.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:46:15-08:00","id":1291679,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you really need Moon\u2019s Hidden Face to hide your forever-wings mutation. Fortunately, it\u2019s a reasonably cheap commitment and easy to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:09:46-08:00","id":1291681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291674#post1291674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be blunt: &quot;I recognize that scar!&quot; as a plot point in a story would almost certainly just make me shake my head and stop reading because it was too dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bully for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Tell basically is a built-in disguise, just with a set difficulty. Of course, by not actually being stated as such it's left to the GM to haphazardly rule on its interactions with any Perception or Awareness Charms that interact with disguises.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Magic that enhances attempts to see through disguises applies on this roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, that was easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Most of the heft&quot; is overselling literally half a sentence out of four paragraphs</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a misleading way to phrase it, considering that only one of those paragraphs disguises mechanics.<br /> <br /> What do you think would be reasonable? A table? A big list of a variety of circumstantial modifiers? Is it really too much of a burden for a Storyteller to figure out that Killfuck Soulshitter reflexively leaping from his throne of skulls to gently help a woman who tripped at his feet back up and inquire after her condition is something that is going to be viewed amiss, can be followed up by the appropriate actions to figure people out, and gets another shot at seeing the Tell with a nice bonus thereafter?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">half of a sentence that doesn't even give concrete mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics of read intentions and profile character are in the core book.<br /> <br /> Other than that, its says to give bonuses higher than three dice to somebody who succeeds on those actions. That sounds pretty concrete for what is ultimately a fairly simple action, so long as one is willing to take a bit of initiative in interpreting the meaning of the word &quot;higher&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the fundamental problem here for me is the text is trying to tie every way to notice a Lunar is out of place to this one mechanic about a physical trait, instead of any kind of more broad rules or guidelines on fitting into the role, whether or not perfect shapechanging is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that primarily rests on the fact that the question of whether or not a Lunar is fitting into the role is both extremely variable depending on the dramatic scenario and... not very complicated?<br /> <br /> What alternative is there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why does Subtle Silver Declaration exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Lunar Charms following the theme of controlling how they're perceived probably ought to address the issue, and still don't eliminate the tension entirely, just shifting some of the odds in their favour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:18:00-08:00","id":1291683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291661#post1291661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tell also lets you carry a mutation between all of your forms.<br /> <br /> Say hello to Mr I-Always-Have-Wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote a big thing arguing this as a misreading, then had the good sense to check back on what the shapeshifting rules say about mutations, where it said in plain black and white that you don't lose mutations tied to the Tell.<br /> <br /> So, yeah you can.<br /> <br /> I suppose that can be offset a bit by making the Tell easier to recognise in other animal forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:23:16-08:00","id":1291686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291683#post1291683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wrote a big thing arguing this as a misreading, then had the good sense to check back on what the shapeshifting rules say about mutations, where it said in plain black and white that you don't lose mutations tied to the Tell.<br /> <br /> So, yeah you can.<br /> <br /> I suppose that can be offset a bit by making the Tell easier to recognise in other animal forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, having Unusual Hide (ooooo) attached to the Tell would make you a bonefide soak monster in animal forms where the Natural Soak is already 13-17. With Moonsilver Light Armor a Boar Toothed Croc would have a resting Soak of 18, 23 with the Armor. <br /> <br /> The Pestletail would have 22, 27 with Armor. O_O<br /> <br /> Edit: Definitely in favour of the Tell now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-24-2019, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:30:38-08:00","id":1291691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291686#post1291686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, having Unusual Hide (ooooo) attached to the Tell would make you a bonefide soak monster in animal forms where the Natural Soak is already 13-17. With Moonsilver Light Armor a Boar Toothed Croc would have a resting Soak of 18, 23 with the Armor.<br /> <br /> The Pestletail would have 22, 27 with Armor. O_O</div> </div> </div> </div>The cost is that the Tell would be obvious in pretty much all shapes without Charms, (and even then..). Unusual Hide 5 is not subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:31:52-08:00","id":1291692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291691#post1291691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cost is that the Tell would be obvious in pretty much all shapes without Charms, (and even then..). Unusual Hide 5 is not subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>For two motes and a starter Charm (Moon\u2019s Hidden Face), it can be (until they see it being used, which I guess is if someone smacks you with a truck and you just brush it off).<br /> <br /> Edit: Time to make Killer Croc!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-24-2019, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:56:17-08:00","id":1291776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1291692#post1291692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Time to make Killer Croc!</div> </div> </div> </div>Make sure and post him to my Rogues Gallery thread when you're done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:19:27-08:00","id":1291841,"title":"","content":"Whenever I hear arguments for or against the Tell, all I can think of is some smarmy Lunar wearing a cattle brand or tattoo or artfully illusory burn scar over it to look like a perfectly normal scarred animal/fashionable bystander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T21:11:22-08:00","id":1292367,"title":"","content":"Here's my initial draft of a replacement mechanic for the Tell that uses carrot instead of stick, tries to get you to actively buy into it despite its downsides a la Infernals, and also acts as a built-in low-key mechanic for chimera weirdness at high Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Warp and Weft:</b><br /> <br /> When using this optional rule, reduce bonus points at character creation to 12 and remove the Tell (<i>Lunars</i>, p. XX), including the ability to associate a mutation with the Tell to apply it to all forms. Instead, at character creation or upon Exalting, a Lunar may choose to gain up to (Essence \u00d7 2) dots of mutations. Each time the Lunar's Essence increases, they may choose to add or upgrade mutations up to this total (even if they had no mutations before). The chosen mutations must either reflect the Lunar's spirit shape in some way (or shapes, with Chimera-Soul Expression) or have been gained temporarily through magic at least once. Each of the chosen mutations automatically gains the Warp merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Warp (0)\u2014Purchased</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Lunar Exalt, one or more permanent mutations.<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Stackable<br /> <br /> Each time you take this merit, choose a different permanent mutation you have. That mutation applies to all of your forms, can't be removed even with potent magic like Wholeness-Restoring Meditation, and can't benefit from the Subtlety merit (<i>Exalted</i>, p. 166) or from magic that directly hides mutations (including Lunar Charms like Moon's Hidden Face).<br /> <br /> Each time you change form, you can attempt to hide one or more of your Warp mutations. This is treated as a reflexive disguise attempt (<i>Exalted</i>, p. 224), with a bonus of (Willpower + Essence) and a penalty of (total mutation dots hidden), but you always roll the average number of successes. Charms can supplement this disguise attempt as normal. As long as you get at least one success, the chosen mutations are hidden similarly to the Subtlety merit, but observers who succeed against the disguise attempt notice or deduce the existence of the hidden mutations.<br /> <br /> If a mutation you choose for this merit is one that you have also selected for an effect like Hybrid Body Transformation, you may immediately re-choose a different temporary mutation or mutations with the same dot total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:17:52-08:00","id":1292422,"title":"","content":"Seems like a fun mechanic, not sure reducing starting BP is the right balance for it, especially if it's an optional feature. For the sake of simplicity and not punishing those who choose not to buy in, wouldn't it be easier to make it a 3 dot Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:20:29-08:00","id":1292424,"title":"","content":"The idea isn't half-bad, but this implementation is clumsy at best. The reflexive disguise roll is just a lengthier process to determine a static value, and I don't see any good reason to make this cost bonus points at chargen or for your Warp mutations to resist the Subtle Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:46:49-08:00","id":1292431,"title":"","content":"This seems even more stick than the existing rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:47:32-08:00","id":1292432,"title":"","content":"I can't recall, do Lunars even have magic to supplement disguise attempts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T04:04:46-08:00","id":1292437,"title":"","content":"There's none in intelligence, which is a bit odd cos that's the attribute you use, but there are appearance charms that aid shapeshifting and there seems to be a tree in Manipulation that deals with it too, if the name Shifting Silver Masquerade is anything to go by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T04:54:13-08:00","id":1292445,"title":"","content":"I think it's because you roll Int+Larceny to make a disguise, cover your body, dye your hair, etc, and all Lunars have for that is your excellency.<br /> <br /> Whereas Lunar charms are literally about changing your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:02:11-08:00","id":1292449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292437#post1292437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if the name Shifting Silver Masquerade is anything to go by.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it something to go by? Where is it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:15:31-08:00","id":1292452,"title":"","content":"It's a Manipulation charm that serves as a totemic alternate prerequisite for Essential Mirror Nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:20:32-08:00","id":1292454,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm looking at this a bit more, and quite apart from the question of &quot;why even model this as a Merit&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292367#post1292367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each time you change form, you can attempt to hide one or more of your Warp mutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it makes anything predicated on the idea of changing form repeatedly and rapidly sound either super inconvenient as it bogs down play with numerous disguise rolls, or something where you're kind of forced to gives up the benefit of having your mutations hidden. I guess any kind of scene in which a Lunar goes through a number of human forms in order to achieve something in short order is right out, or at least extremely awkward and difficult. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is treated as a reflexive disguise attempt (<i>Exalted</i>, p. 224), with a bonus of (Willpower + Essence) and a penalty of (total mutation dots hidden), but you always roll the average number of successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this line even mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mutation you choose for this merit is one that you have also selected for an effect like Hybrid Body Transformation, you may immediately re-choose a different temporary mutation or mutations with the same dot total.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does this work? Are you getting to acquire new mutations wholesale? Was a mutation that previously wasn't hidden now is? What would the point of that be, since people have presumably already seen the mutation that you're now hiding? And then when you transform back, that mutation becomes exposed again?<br /> <br /> I mean, the mutations you're required to take have to be for your spirit shape, but the disguise roll is penalised by how many you're hiding at once, so you're kind of discouraged from hiding many (which seems to kind of contradict the point of hiding them at all)\u2026 and your hybrid body <i>also</i> needs to base mutations on your spirit shape, and there are probably only so many mutations that a given animal will afford, so there's going to be a lot of overlap... so when you change form, a hidden mutation will... no, wait, why would anybody give their hybrid form a mutation that they already have?<br /> <br /> What <i>is</i> the carrot here? Two dots of mutations at character creation? You could buy more than that for the bonus points that you're saying to take away!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:30:11-08:00","id":1292457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292367#post1292367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my initial draft of a replacement mechanic for the Tell that uses carrot instead of stick\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>How is the Tell as-is a stick? The whole purpose of the carrot and stick analogy is to show how a given thing tries to get you to express a certain behavior; you use carrots and sticks to get a donkey to <i>move</i>. What sort of behavior is the Tell supposed to incentivize you towards?<br /> <br /> Sometimes a trait is a trait, rather than some reward-or-punishment-based incentive system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:38:50-08:00","id":1292464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292454#post1292454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does this line even mean?</div> </div> </div> </div> As far as I can tell, you form a pool of (Intelligence + Larceny + Willpower + Essence), with a penalty equal to the dot value of the mutations you want to hide. You can enhance this with magic that supplements a disguise, but instead of rolling, you take the average. That would <i>usually</i> mean half your pool, but with Charms that double nines or reroll certain failed dice...<br /> <br /> In short: it's an awkward, constantly shifting static value, like the difficulty to spot the Tell but with extra work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:03:33-08:00","id":1292487,"title":"","content":"If you don't like the Tell and want a house rule, just say Lunars don't have Tells, but have ST permission to buy mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:28:01-08:00","id":1292495,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think what's needed isn't a replacement system <i>for the Tell</i> but just a way of scaling the difficulty to spot the Tell through favorable circumstances and disguise attempts. As it stands, the main problem is that ANY disguise attempt for a Lunar, no matter how well they roll, has its effective successes capped at 7, barring magic such as Subtle Silver Declaration. I don't think this lends itself very well to a high-tension scene of cat-and-mouse where the roles can switch at any time, because the mechanics-facing solution is always to just roll more Awareness successes. Of course, neither does just scaling the difficulty - I'd love to see a dedicated subsystem for spycraft and infiltration, one with more complexity than &quot;Whoever gets the most successes wins&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:36:18-08:00","id":1292499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292495#post1292495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think what's needed isn't a replacement system <i>for the Tell</i> but just a way of scaling the difficulty to spot the Tell through favorable circumstances and disguise attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... people get bonus successes from having seen the Tell before (probably from the anima) and bonus dice from the Lunar acting out of character and somebody reading or profiling them. It's more than nothing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:07:04-08:00","id":1292540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292499#post1292499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like... people get bonus successes from having seen the Tell before (probably from the anima) and bonus dice from the Lunar acting out of character and somebody reading or profiling them. It's more than nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant on the Lunar's side of things. Characters trying to detect a disguised Lunar's Tell have ways to narrow their search and get clues that aren't just binary pass/fail, and these are through <i>actions</i> they can take in play. The Lunar, meanwhile, has little recourse against someone who knows their Tell because detecting it obviates <i>all </i>forms of disguise, not just shapeshifting. Granted, it's a little ambiguous as to whether secondhand knowledge qualifies someone to roll (ie have heard or read about you from someone who DID see your Tell in person) - if not, a Lunar should be okay with just eliminating enemies who make them, but if so then that points toward having to kill <i>anyone </i>who knows their Tell to keep that information secret.<br /> <br /> Given the potential for player/ST expectations misaligning and <i>explosively</i>-derailing a chronicle, it would be good to have some clarification of authorial intent and ways to address these situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:39:22-08:00","id":1292574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292464#post1292464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As far as I can tell, you form a pool of (Intelligence + Larceny + Willpower + Essence), with a penalty equal to the dot value of the mutations you want to hide. You can enhance this with magic that supplements a disguise, but instead of rolling, you take the average. That would <i>usually</i> mean half your pool, but with Charms that double nines or reroll certain failed dice...<br /> <br /> In short: it's an awkward, constantly shifting static value, like the difficulty to spot the Tell but with extra work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a clunky attempt at making a static-value-except-in-name, to try to avoid mechanical incompatibility with other stuff that would apply to rolls but not static values. It's probably not worth the hassle compared to making it a static value that just gets a dots-of-mutations-to-hide penalty, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T13:05:36-08:00","id":1292582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292540#post1292540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, it's a little ambiguous as to whether secondhand knowledge qualifies someone to roll (ie have heard or read about you from someone who DID see your Tell in person) - if not, a Lunar should be okay with just eliminating enemies who make them, but if so then that points toward having to kill <i>anyone </i>who knows their Tell to keep that information secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could move.<br /> <br /> I think your idea that having the Tell see through one form makes it visible in all of them is a misreading. I think that if somebody makes you, you scurry away as a mouse and re-enter the scene in a different human shape, they have to roll all over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T16:11:58-08:00","id":1292639,"title":"","content":"Second hand wouldn't work for the bonus on detecting a Lunar's tell. It explicitly says, &quot;Character's who've previously successfully detected the Lunar's Tell receive 3 bonus dice.&quot; So the odds go up on them spotting your tell a second time after they've seen it the first time. That said it is a far cry from the implication that someone noticing that pigeon has been really quiet and still while you've been talking has a freaking peacock eye pattern on its tail feathers, would immediately spot the tell on their forearm when they come out of the bathroom as some random person. Also the bonus does not pass on through education, doesn't matter if its a common story and every one in the world knows that Raksi's fingers bend backwards the check would still apply as per normal unless the person seen through it before.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;can obviate the difficulty of noticing a Tell&quot; thing. Due to the variety of Tells, how they appear on different forms, and the number of potential forms a Lunar can potentially be wearing, creating a system to explicitly reveal and make obvious a Tell even if the person has never seen it would be insanely difficult even assuming you had the system designed by someone who's seen it before and knows for a fact which Lunar will be showing up. And the Lunar would know their Tell and how it manifests in their form unless they've only recently acquired it. So if you know how your Tell is going to manifest in a form and you don't want to risk it being noticed then you'd know how you could go about hiding it. (See countless creatures with tails pretending the tail is a belt, or Blake from RWBY wearing a ribbon to make her cat ears look like a bow.) Not even counting my favorite lie to cover weird crap about one's form, &quot;Ugh sorcerery.&quot; And all of this is operating off the assumption that you have assumed this form and are stuck in a situation where you're right there in the open to be analyzed as opposed to just one of the many birds in the person's menagerie that they haven't noticed is extra and that if you look closely you'll notice the patterns on its feathers look a lot like the suction cups on an octopus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 02-27-2019, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:04:25-08:00","id":1292658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292639#post1292639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said it is a far cry from the implication that someone noticing that pigeon has been really quiet and still while you've been talking has a freaking peacock eye pattern on its tail feathers, would immediately spot the tell on their forearm when they come out of the bathroom as some random person.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Success lets them notice the Tell, or, if they\u2019ve noticed it before in a different form, identify her as the same individual.&quot; So if that second roll is a success, yes, they know the person who came out of the bathroom is the same person as the pigeon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292639#post1292639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you know how your Tell is going to manifest in a form and you don't want to risk it being noticed then you'd know how you could go about hiding it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the devs, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1291411#post1291411\">that's not an option</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292454#post1292454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like it makes anything predicated on the idea of changing form repeatedly and rapidly sound either super inconvenient as it bogs down play with numerous disguise rolls, or something where you're kind of forced to gives up the benefit of having your mutations hidden. I guess any kind of scene in which a Lunar goes through a number of human forms in order to achieve something in short order is right out, or at least extremely awkward and difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing actually prevents you in the existing disguise rules from spending 5 minutes at a time until you coincidentally roll the maximum on all your dice, so I don't have any existing no-that's-stupid framework to lean on. Just making a static rating would simplify things, but also leads to the &quot;how do you apply double 9s to that&quot; question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292454#post1292454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how does this work? Are you getting to acquire new mutations wholesale? Was a mutation that previously wasn't hidden now is? What would the point of that be, since people have presumably already seen the mutation that you're now hiding? And then when you transform back, that mutation becomes exposed again?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just a clause to keep you from being screwed out of a Hybrid Body Transformation mutation dot forever because you picked Tail for it and then later gained it as a Warp mutation. The wording is hampered because there's no standard templating for this stuff, but the intent is that you just replace the selection in the Charm completely with whatever the new thing you pick is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292454#post1292454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the mutations you're required to take have to be for your spirit shape, but the disguise roll is penalised by how many you're hiding at once, so you're kind of discouraged from hiding many (which seems to kind of contradict the point of hiding them at all)\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike the Tell, however, seeing any of the mutations doesn't give away your identity to that person forever, so there's not actually a huge downside (other than the obvious issues of being a beastman) to hide only the weirdest mutations and leave a fox tail on display.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292454#post1292454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and your hybrid body <i>also</i> needs to base mutations on your spirit shape, and there are probably only so many mutations that a given animal will afford, so there's going to be a lot of overlap...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably confident that I can get at least 10 dots of thematically appropriate mutations out of any spirit shape you can name, and if you're reaching for ideas at higher Essence that's the reason you can start dipping into weird chimeric stuff with the &quot;temporarily gained from magic&quot; clause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292454#post1292454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so when you change form, a hidden mutation will... no, wait, why would anybody give their hybrid form a mutation that they already have?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the reason for the &quot;it doesn't screw you out of a dot&quot; clause, above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What <i>is</i> the carrot here? Two dots of mutations at character creation? You could buy more than that for the bonus points that you're saying to take away! </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe carrot is that either:<br /> <br /> a) You don't take any of the free mutations, and you effectively get Subtle Silver Declaration-but-better for 3 BP, since you never have to deal with a Tell or similar mechanic.<br /> <br /> b) You take the free mutations, and you get up to +7 BP worth in the long run as recompense for the problems with hiding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:08:28-08:00","id":1292662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292658#post1292658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if that second roll is a success, yes, they know the person who came out of the bathroom is the same person as the pigeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still requires they need to succeed on that roll a second time, which still isn't a given.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:15:48-08:00","id":1292666,"title":"","content":"I suppose it's consistent, although I certainly think the wording would need to be cleaned up a bit, and even then it seems a bit convoluted with regards to hybrid body matters.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't work for me, because I actively like the Tell, and the mythology, characterisation and story scenarios it entails, but I can see it being desirable to people that don't, or are maybe looking for an alternative version of the trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:28:56-08:00","id":1292670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292662#post1292662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still requires they need to succeed on that roll a second time, which still isn't a given.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but if they're rolling 14 dice against a <i>pigeon</i> I would find it unsurprising that they could roll 11 dice against a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:30:55-08:00","id":1292681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292670#post1292670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but if they're rolling 14 dice against a <i>pigeon</i> I would find it unsurprising that they could roll 11 dice against a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay you are aware that's pretty close to a nightmare scenario right? Remember 14 dice is not something that gets swung around by well pretty much anything that isn't magic. Even Exalts, your biggest threat when it comes to someone spotting your Tell, would need to burn motes get their dicepool there. Now this is far from impossible, but it does lose a bit that you're arguing that the Tell is a major flaw that completely invalidates a Lunar's shapeshifting when you present the idea as if it fails against any competent observer when your argument views any competent observer as defined by people using magic to see through disguises. *<br /> <br /> Also your citation of the dev doesn't work as a counter. Vance's statement was that without charm use you can't make it impossible for them to roll to detect, doesn't mean you can't run the scenario to make it harder for them to get that view on you. Just saying your argument is that people can take actions in game to make it harder for a Lunar to hide or effectively use then by the same token the Lunar is allowed to take actions to make it harder than normal for them to spot the Tell. <br /> <br /> Granted the big thing is no having your Tell spotted once does not immediately make it so you are automatically identified to that person forever and ever. Think about the goal in making these abilities, this would be an invalidation almost on par with the whole Non-abyssal Exalts can't regain motes in the Underworld, Abyssal's can't regain out of the Underworld and also can't use hearthstones unless they're in a soulsteel amulet. Afterall your Tell becomes obvious at either mid or high level anima banner, meaning one flare at that level would could invalidate your shapeshifting to god only knows how many people forever if you went with the idea that seeing the Tell once meant they could automatically see through it regardless of form.<br /> <br /> *Remember entities considered trivial don't even get to make the roll to spot your Tell, so the only people making this check are people deemed as potential threats to whatever you're doing by the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:34:22-08:00","id":1292682,"title":"","content":"Mm, dropping in my two cents: I like the mechanics for the Tell this edition. I think, leaving aside any finnicky edge cases, it's realized in a way that enforces an evocative genre conceit of shapeshifters like Lunars, but doesn't compromise their mythic abilities in subterfuge and disguise. It's just difficult enough that most people can't meaningfully oppose it, but heroic actors and characters that matter have a chance to expose you through your iconic trait, though it's not easy.<br /> <br /> Subtle Silver Declaration is essentially a cost you can pay to <i>not</i> engage in the genre convention, which handily builds off into powers that reinforce the talent of Lunars in subtlety and deception, and grants Changing Moons (and others) something to build up from which justifies their focus as the experts in stealth and misdirection within the splat.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think its place in the game comes together rather well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:43:30-08:00","id":1292685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292670#post1292670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but if they're rolling 14 dice against a <i>pigeon</i> I would find it unsurprising that they could roll 11 dice against a person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As noted, the person who's rolling 11 dice to begin with is likely Batman, so honestly him noticing something weird about that pigeon isn't surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T20:06:57-08:00","id":1292688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289791-why-bring-back-the-tell-again?p=1292682#post1292682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Subtle Silver Declaration is essentially a cost you can pay to <i>not</i> engage in the genre convention</div> </div> </div> </